.TH APPLESOYLICON 1 "October 2026" "applesoylicon 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
applesoylicon \- animated terminal rain with accelerometer-driven physics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B applesoylicon
.RI [ WORD ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B applesoylicon --setup
.RI KEY=VALUE ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B applesoylicon
draws animated character rain in an interactive terminal.
The optional
.I WORD
is displayed inside the rain.  The default word is APPLESOYLICON.
.PP
Rain can use a fixed cardinal direction or react continuously to raw Linux IIO
accelerometer readings.  Gyro mode applies the device mount matrix and simulates
acceleration, inertia, drag, terminal velocity, trails, and screen-edge wrapping.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--direction " DIR
Set a fixed direction to
.BR down ,
.BR up ,
.BR left ,
or
.BR right .
The value
.B auto
enables physical sensor mode.  The default is
.BR down .
.TP
.B --gyro
Enable physical rain driven by raw Linux IIO acceleration.  This is equivalent
to
.BR "--direction auto" .
.TP
.BI "--gyro-offset " DEG
Rotate the mounted sensor vector clockwise by 0, 90, 180, or 270 degrees.
This corrects installations where the display has a persistent rotation that
does not match the accelerometer mount orientation.
.TP
.BI "--palette " NAME
Select
.BR green ,
.BR amber ,
.BR ice ,
or
.BR soy .
The default is
.BR green .
.TP
.BI "--fps " N
Set the frame rate from 5 through 60.  The default is 24.
.TP
.BI "--density " N
Set rain density from 0.05 through 1.0.  In physical mode this controls the
particle count.  The default is 0.72.
.TP
.BI "--message " TEXT
Set the displayed word explicitly.  This is an alias for the positional
.IR WORD .
The value must contain 1 through 40 ASCII characters.
.TP
.BI "--seed " N
Use a deterministic unsigned integer random seed.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Display command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.BI "--setup " KEY=VALUE...
Validate and save one or more persistent defaults.  Supported keys are
.BR palette ,
.BR fps ,
.BR density ,
.BR message ,
.BR seed ,
.BR direction ,
.BR gyro ,
and
.BR gyro-offset .
Command-line options override saved values.
.TP
.B --setup show
Print the configuration path and saved values.
.TP
.B --setup reset
Remove all saved values and restore built-in defaults.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR q , " Esc" , " Ctrl-C"
Exit and restore the terminal.
.TP
.BR [ " / " ]
Decrease or increase rain density.
.TP
.B r
Rotate a fixed rain direction clockwise.  Physical sensor mode ignores this
key.
.TP
.B p
Cycle through the color palettes.
.TP
.BR + " / " -
Increase or decrease animation speed.
.TP
.B d
Toggle between sparse and dense rain.
.SH SENSOR MODE
Sensor mode searches
.I /sys/bus/iio/devices
for a readable device exposing
.IR in_accel_x_raw ,
.IR in_accel_y_raw ,
and
.IR in_accel_z_raw .
If available,
.I in_accel_mount_matrix
is applied before the values enter the simulation.  Readings are sampled at
40 Hz and low-pass filtered.
.PP
If no compatible readable accelerometer exists, use a fixed
.B --direction
instead.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run soy-colored rain with the default word:
.PP
.EX
applesoylicon --palette soy
.EE
.PP
Show a custom word and fall to the left:
.PP
.EX
applesoylicon APPLE --direction left
.EE
.PP
Use physical acceleration with sparse rain:
.PP
.EX
applesoylicon SOY --gyro --density 0.25
.EE
.PP
Persist sensor correction and preferred defaults:
.PP
.EX
applesoylicon --setup gyro-offset=90 gyro=true palette=soy density=0.4
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:device*/in_accel_*_raw
Raw accelerometer channels used by physical sensor mode.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/applesoylicon/config
Persistent defaults.  If XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset, the path is
.IR $HOME/.config/applesoylicon/config .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 on runtime failure, and 2 for invalid command-line
arguments.
